{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_36","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'tmpbase=\"${TMPDIR:-/var/folders}\"; i=0; for u in '\"'https://www.mangalayatan.ac.in/department-of-agriculture/b-sc-h-agriculture/' 'https://www.mangalayatan.ac.in/department-of-agriculture/b-sc-hons-forestry/' 'https://www.mangalayatan.ac.in/department-of-agriculture/b-sc-hons-horticulture/' 'https://www.mangalayatan.ac.in/department-of-agriculture/diploma-in-agriculture/' 'https://www.mangalayatan.ac.in/department-of-agriculture/masters-of-science-agriculture/' 'https://www.mangalayatan.ac.in/department-of-agriculture/m-sc-forestry/' 'https://www.mangalayatan.ac.in/department-of-agriculture/m-sc-horticulture/'; do i=\"'$((i+1)); out=\"$tmpbase/mu_ag_detail_$i.html\"; curl --insecure -L --fail --silent --show-error --max-time 30 -A '\"'Mozilla/5.0' \\\"\"'$u\" -o \"$out\" || continue; echo \"--- $u ---\"; python3 -c '\"'from bs4 import BeautifulSoup; import sys; s=BeautifulSoup(open(sys.argv[1],encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\",errors=\\\"ignore\\\"),\\\"html.parser\\\"); [x.decompose() for x in s([\\\"script\\\",\\\"style\\\",\\\"noscript\\\",\\\"svg\\\",\\\"nav\\\",\\\"header\\\",\\\"footer\\\"])]; root=s.find(\\\"main\\\") or s.find(\\\"article\\\") or s.body; out=[]; [out.append(\\\" \\\".join(x.get_text(\\\" \\\",strip=True).split())) for x in root.find_all([\\\"title\\\",\\\"h1\\\",\\\"h2\\\",\\\"h3\\\",\\\"h4\\\",\\\"h5\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"li\\\",\\\"td\\\",\\\"th\\\"])]; print(\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\".join([x for x in out if x and len(x)<500])[:7000])' \\\"\"'$out\" | head -90; done'","aggregated_output":"--- https://www.mangalayatan.ac.in/department-of-agriculture/b-sc-h-agriculture/ ---\nDuration\\n4 years undergraduate professional degree\\nEligibility\\nPassed 10+2 (PCB/ PCM) with minimum 50% marks\\nFees\\nTotal 72,000/- Year INR Only\\nB.Sc. (H) Agriculture\\nProgramme Overview\\nCandidate seeking admission to B.Sc. (H) Agriculture program should have passed 10+2 (PCB/ PCM) with minimum 50% marks or equivalent grade from a recognize Board or Institutions.\\nFollowing are some government sector organizations which have job opportunities for agriculture graduates:-\\nIndian Agricultural Research Institute\\nNational Seeds Corporation Limited\\nState Farms Corporation of India\\nFood Corporation of India\\nNational Dairy Development Board\\nNABARD and other banks\\nAgricultural finance corporations\\nIndian Council of Agricultural Research\\nCouncil of Scientific and Industrial Research\\nNorth Eastern Region Agricultural Marketing Corporation\\nFollowing are the private sectors which offer jobs to agriculture graduates:-\\nAgro-industries\\nAgriculture Marketing\\nFinancial sector with the focus on agriculture\\nMicro-finance institutions\\nFertilizer companies\\nAgri-biotech organizations\\nSome of the best agro-based products’ companies that offer jobs to B.Sc. (H) Agriculture graduates, are:-\\nDuPont India\\nRallies India Limited\\nAdvanta Limited\\nNational Agro Industries\\nRaasi Seeds\\nABT Industries\\nPhalada Agro Research Foundation Limited.\\nSome of the jobs offered to B.Sc. (H)Agriculture graduates:-\\nSeed Technologist\\nAgriculture Officer\\nAssistant Plantation Manager\\nAgricultural Research Scientist\\nAgriculture Development Officer\\nAgriculture Technician\\nMarketing Executive\\nRice Breeder\\nAssistant Manager (Tea and Rubber Plantation)\\nAssistant Manager (Cocoa, Teak, Indigo, Tobacco, Jute and pepper plantation)\\nLand Geomatics Surveyor\\nSoil Forestry Officer\\nSoil Quality Officer\\nPlant Breeder/Grafting expert\\nSeed/Nursery Manager\\nBudding/Tissue culture expert\\nAssistant Manager (Horticulture)\\nNote:- The average salary offered depends on the area or industry the student is working for. Basic salary after completion of this program ranges from 15K to 20K per month depending upon various factors like profile, industry, etc.\\nWhy Choose Mangalayatan University, Jabalpur for B.Sc )H) Agriculture\\nAgriculture experts develop new methods of organic farming and promote them so that our farmers adopt chemical-free crop production practices.\\nThis program focuses on teaching students how to prosper in agriculture using modern scientific equipment and techniques, covering aspects of water resource management, land surveying, soil sciences, and poultry management among various others. The main objective of the program is to teach students how to improve agricultural productivity.\\nAgricultural education is a broad discipline which includes branches / fields like:\\nAgriculture (Agronomy)\\nVeterinary Science\\nForestry\\nFisheries\\nHorticulture\\nHome Science\\nB.Sc. (H) Agriculture Program Curriculum/Subjects\\nAgronomy\\nHorticulture\\nPlant Pathology\\nEntomology\\nAgricultural Economics\\nExtension education,\\nGenetics and Plant Breeding\\nSoil Science,\\nFood Technology\\nAnimal Husbandry\\nBasic Sciences, Humanities, and Agricultural Engineering\\nDownload Complete Course Curriculum\\nCareer Prospects and Scope After B.Sc (H) Agriculture\\nThe graduates of this degree program can find jobs in both the public and private sectors. The agriculture sector in India is expanding rapidly their by opening new avenues in this field as well as in the various allied fields\\nFrequently Asked Questions (FAQs)\\nThe program is a 4-year undergraduate degree.\\nStudents learn crop production, soil science, agricultural economics, plant breeding, and modern farming techniques.\\nYes. Field visits, agricultural projects, and hands-on farm training are integral parts of the program.\\nYes. Students can pursue an M.Sc. in Agriculture and other specialized agricultural programs.\\nGraduates can work in agribusiness, agricultural research, government departments, food industries, and farm management.\\nLife @ Mangalayatan University, Jabalpur\\nIndustry oriented Curriculum\\nGlobally recognised Programs\\nEco-Friendly Big Campus\\nEminent faculty from Academia & Industry\\nDigital Classroom & Wi-fi Campus\\nUpto 100% Scholarship for meritorious Students\\nIndoor & Outdoor Sports facility\\nCentrally AC Classrooms\\nDynamic Placement Cell\\nScholarships & Stipend from Government\\nCore values Adherence & Disciplined Environment\\nDigital Classroom & Wi-fi Campus\\nExcellent Library, Laboratories at Hi-tech Computer Labs\\nIndustrial / Educational Tour for hands-on Learning\n--- https://www.mangalayatan.ac.in/department-of-agriculture/b-sc-hons-forestry/ ---\nDuration\\n4 years undergraduate professional degree\\nEligibility\\nPassed 10+2 (PCB/ PCM) with minimum 50% marks\\nFees\\nTotal 72,000/- Year INR Only\\nAbout B.Sc (Hons.) Forestry\\nSome major subjects taught in B.sc (Hons) Forestry areFundamentals of Geology and Soil Science, Plant Biochemistry and Biotechnology, Introductory Botany, Basic Mathematics, Principles of Plant physiology, Elementary Statistic and Computer Application, Chemistry and Fertility of Soils, Wood Science and Technology, etc.\\nAgro industries\\nAgriculture Marketing\\nFinancial sector with focus on agriculture\\nMicro-finance institutions\\nFertilizer companies\\nAgri-biotech organizations\\nIndian Agricultural Research Institute\\nNational Seeds Corporation Limited\\nState Farms Corporation of India\\nFood Corporation of India\\nNational Dairy Development Board\\nNABARD and other banks\\nAgricultural finance corporations\\nIndian Council of Agricultural Research\\nCouncil of Scientific and Industrial Research\\nNorth Eastern Region Agricultural Marketing Corporation\\nUpon completion of B.sc (Hons) Forestry, candidates can go for higher studies like M.sc Forestry, MBA, MCA, etc.\\nCandidates who have B.sc (Hons) Forestry degree, can prepare for coveted government examinations like UPSC, SSC CGL, Bank PO and India Railways\\nCandidates can appear in Indian Forest Service examination, which is conducted by UPSC\\nForestry Research Institutes that come under the Indian Council of Forestry Research and Education, release exclusive vacancies for B.sc (Hons) Forestry graduates\\nWhy Choose Mangalayatan University Jabalpur for B. Sc (Hons) Forestry?\\nMangalayatan University Jabalpur is the best University in Jabalpur, highly acclaimed and coveted for higher education in the domain of agriculture and its allied areas\\nThe programme exposes students to practical forestry management experience and high-quality applied researchthat aims to bring positive change to the natural world\\nThe programme equips students with excellent technical acumen and problem-solving skills which make them globally competitive and inspires for higher studies, research and development\\nStudents get Hands-on Training (HOT) and internship opportunities at forest research institutes\\nelit. Ut elit tellus, luctus nec ullamcorper mattis, pulvinar dapibus leo.\\nCareer Prospects and Scope of B.sc (Hons) Forestry:\\nUpon completion of B.sc (Hons) Forestry, candidates can go for higher studies like M.sc Forestry, MBA, MCA, etc.\\nCandidates who have B.sc (Hons) Forestry degree, can prepare for coveted government examinations like UPSC, SSC CGL, Bank PO and India Railways\\nCandidates can appear in Indian Forest Service examination, which is conducted by UPSC\\nForestry Research Institutes that come under the Indian Council of Forestry Research and Education, release exclusive vacancies for B.sc (Hons) Forestry graduates\\nGovernment Employment Opportunities for B.sc (Hons) Forestry:\\nIndian Agricultural Research Institute\\nNational Seeds Corporation Limited\\nState Farms Corporation of India\\nFood Corporation of India\\nNational Dairy Development Board\\nNABARD and other banks\\nAgricultural finance corporations\\nIndian Council of Agricultural Research\\nCouncil of Scientific and Industrial Research\\nNorth Eastern Region Agricultural Marketing Corporation\\nPrivate Employment Opportunities for B.sc (Hons) Forestry:\\nAgro industries\\nAgriculture Marketing\\nFinancial sector with focus on agriculture\\nMicro-finance institutions\\nFertilizer companies\\nAgri-biotech organizations\\nFrequently Asked Questions (FAQs)\\nThe program focuses on forest management, wildlife conservation, biodiversity, and environmental sustainability.\\nThe B.Sc. (Hons.) Forestry program is typically 4 years long.\\nYes. Students participate in forest surveys, field visits, and practical conservation activities.\\nYes. Growing environmental concerns have increased demand for forestry and conservation professionals.\\nGraduates can work in forest departments, wildlife organizations, NGOs, environmental agencies, and research institutions.\\nFacilities\\nIndustry oriented Curriculum\\nGlobally recognised Programs\\nEco-Friendly Big Campus\\nEminent faculty from Academia & Industry\\nDigital Classroom & Wi-fi Campus\\nUpto 100% Scholarship for meritorious Students\\nIndoor & Outdoor Sports facility\\nCentrally AC Classrooms\\nDynamic Placement Cell\\nScholarships & Stipend from Government\\nCore values Adherence & Disciplined Environment\\nDigital Classroom & Wi-fi Campus\\nExcellent Library, Laboratories at Hi-tech Computer Labs\\nIndustrial / Educational Tour for hands-on Learning\n--- https://www.mangalayatan.ac.in/department-of-agriculture/b-sc-hons-horticulture/ ---\nDuration\\n4 years undergraduate professional degree\\nEligibility\\nPassed 10+2 (PCB/ PCM) with minimum 50% marks\\nFees\\nTotal 72,000/- Year INR Only\\nAbout B.Sc (Hons.) horticulture\\nThe opening of global trade in the horticulture sector has encouraged manyto diversify their activities with horticulture crops and also created a great demand of professionals to help in the development of the horticulture sector in the country. Keeping this thing in mind, Mangalayatan University Jabalpur has started a full-fledgedfour year undergraduate programme B.sc (Hons) Horticulture.\\nWhy Choose Mangalayatan University Jabalpur for B. Sc (Hons) Horticulture?\\nMangalayatan University Jabalpur is the best University in Jabalpur, highly acclaimed and coveted for higher education in the domain of agriculture and its allied areas.\\nThe programme exposes students to the real lifestyle in areas such as agriculture and livelihood systems, the socio-economic conditions of the farmers, and their problems that relate to modern agricultural development.\\nThe programme equips students with excellent technical acumen and problem-solving skills which make them globally competitive and inspires for higher studies and entrepreneurship development.\\nStudents get Hands-on Training (HOT) and internship opportunities at agriculture-based companies, rural cottage industries, research institutions and service-providing extension institutions\\nStudents get the opportunity to participate in all India and state education toursthat provide exposure to State Agricultural Universities and ICAR governed research institutions and their functioning.\\nCareer Prospects and Scope of B.sc (Hons) Horticulture:\\nUpon completion of B.sc (Hons) Horticulture, candidate can go for higher studies like M.sc Horticulture, MBA, MCA, etc.\\nCandidates who have B.sc (Hons) Horticulture degree, can prepare for coveted government examinations like UPSC, SSC CGL, Bank PO and India Railways\\nAgricultural research institutes like Indian Council of Agricultural Research- New Delhi, Central Potato Research Institute- Shimla, Indian Institute of Horticulture Research- Bangalore release exclusive vacancies for B.sc (Hons) Horticulture graduates\\nThe career opportunities for horticulturists range from commercial, environmental sectors to research as well as journalism.\\nGovernment Employment Opportunities for B.sc (Hons) Horticulture:\\nIndian Agricultural Research Institute\\nNational Seeds Corporation Limited\\nState Farms Corporation of India\\nFood Corporation of India\\nCentral Institute of Cotton Research\\nNABARD and other banks\\nPrivate Employment Opportunities for B.sc (Hons) Horticulture:\\nAgro-industries\\nHorticulture Marketing\\nFinancial sector with the focus on agriculture\\nMicro-finance institutions\\nFertilizer companies\\nAgri-biotech organizations\\nFrequently Asked Questions (FAQs)\\nHorticulture focuses on the cultivation of fruits, vegetables, flowers, medicinal plants, and landscaping.\\nThe B.Sc. (Hons.) Horticulture program generally lasts 4 years.\\nYes. Students receive extensive training through nurseries, gardens, fieldwork, and laboratory sessions.\\nYes. Many graduates establish nurseries, landscaping businesses, or horticulture ventures.\\nCareer options include horticulture officer, nursery manager, landscape designer, consultant, and researcher.\\nFacilities\\nIndustry oriented Curriculum\\nGlobally recognised Programs\\nEco-Friendly Big Campus\\nEminent faculty from Academia & Industry\\nDigital Classroom & Wi-fi Campus\\nUpto 100% Scholarship for meritorious Students\\nIndoor & Outdoor Sports facility\\nCentrally AC Classrooms\\nDynamic Placement Cell\\nScholarships & Stipend from Government\\nCore values Adherence & Disciplined Environment\\nDigital Classroom & Wi-fi Campus\\nExcellent Library, Laboratories at Hi-tech Computer Labs\\nIndustrial / Educational Tour for hands-on Learning\n--- https://www.mangalayatan.ac.in/department-of-agriculture/diploma-in-agriculture/ ---\nDuration\\n2 year which consists of 2 semesters\\nEligibility\\n10+2 or Equivalent in Agriculture or Science\\nFees\\nTotal 30,000 / Year INR Only\\nAbout Programme\\nTo be honest, qualified professionals are always valued, when it comes to agriculture sector. Thus, it is evident that there is more than just one reason to pursue this course!\\nWhy MUJ for this course\\nMangalayatan University has been established to nurture and polish the knowledge of all its students to reach heights of success. The programs in Agriculture are envisaged to be the best professional programs offered by the University. For this, the University has hired highly experienced faculty and offers state-of-the-art infrastructure, with an active placement cell to boost the career prospects of the aspiring students.\\nProgram Overview\\nThe program provides updated knowledge base and imparts required technical skills so that the students may pursue successful career in agriculture sector.\\nThis program covers animal science, food production, horticulture, environmental preservation, basic sciences like Botany and Zoology and other aspects of Agriculture Science. The agriculture sector with its immense potential can provide many career opportunities for candidates who wish to take up agriculture business and other allied activities.\\nIn order to sustain, diversify and realize the full potential of agriculture sector, it would be necessary to develop skilled human resources. Modern agriculture being a highly dynamic process, human resource development in this field is a continuous process that is undertaken by Agricultural Universities and institutions. Agricultural Universities impart education in the various core and allied fields of Agriculture.\\nDiploma in Agriculture program aims towards:\\nImparting knowledge of Agriculture and its allied fields\\nFacilitating study of agriculture forestry, livestock and other allied fields required to raise the income of farmers\\nDissemination of various techniques of farming and farming system in India\\nStudy of market and marketing of agricultural produce.\\nThis programme will also help in enhancing students’ employability\\nTo enhance an understanding of the impact of globalization and diversity on\\nStudents will be able to understand and analyze the current developments in agriculture and how they affect their future in agriculture.\\nStudents will be able to recognize and examine the relationships between inputs and outputs in their agricultural field to make effective and profitable decisions.\\nStudents will understand how all aspects of agriculture combine and are used by scientists, marketers, and producers.\\nStudents will be able to demonstrate critical thinking and problem solving skills as they apply the same to a variety of animal and or plant production systems.\\nA wide range of job opportunities is available for Diploma holders in Agriculture. One can find employment in both public and private sectors. One can also be self-employed which has immense potential for growth.\\nAgricultural science involves research and development on production, processing, productivity of crops and end products for consumers etc.. Major activities include improving the quality and quantity of farming, improving crop yield, minimizing labor, conservation of soil and water and pest control. Interested diploma holder in Agriculture may opt for further studies in the field e.g. B.Sc(H) Agriculture, M.Sc Agriculture and Ph.D. and subsequently pursue a career in agricultural research.\\nThe agriculture sector is not only about scientific research and development. It provides roles for students with business backgrounds as well.\\nThere are many opportunities in the agriculture sector for an experienced agricultural professional. These professionals may get opportunities in major areas like:\\nFood production firms\\nGovernment agricultural firms\\nBanks\\nPlantations\\nGovernment fertilizer manufacturing firms\\nPrivate fertilizer manufacturing firms\\nAgriculture machinery manufacturing firms\\nProfessionals may work as agricultural engineer, agricultural inspector, agricultural ecologist, conservation planner, fishery manager, the plant biologist, water conservationist, agricultural manager, botanist, horticulturist, plant ecologist, etc. Some professionals may also take up teaching in both private and government schools, colleges & universities.\\nCandidates who have passed the Class XII examination in Science stream (Physics, Chemistry & Maths/Biology) or an equivalent examination from a recognized board with minimum 50% marks or equivalent grade are eligible for admission to this program. Eligible candidates may apply for this program through online or offline modes.\\nDiploma in Agriculture is a one year program which can be pursued by a student who is interested in taking up agriculture as his/her profession. The duration of the program is 1 year which consists of 2 semesters.\\nFAQ's\\nThe program provides updated knowledge base and imparts required technical skills so that the students may pursue successful career in agriculture sector.\\nThis program covers animal science, food production, horticulture, environmental preservation, basic sciences like Botany and Zoology and other aspects of Agriculture Science. The agriculture sector with its immense potential can provide many career opportunities for candidates who wish to take up agriculture business and other allied activities.\\nIn order to sustain, diversify and realize the full potential of agriculture sector, it would be necessary to develop skilled human resources. Modern agriculture being a highly dynamic process, human resource development in this field is a continuous process that is undertaken by Agricultural Universities and institutions. Agricultural Universities impart education in the various core and allied fields of Agriculture.\\nDiploma in Agriculture program aims towards:\\nImparting knowledge of Agriculture and its allied fields\\nFacilitating study of agriculture forestry, livestock and other allied fields required to raise the income of farmers\\nDissemination of various techniques of farming and farming system in India\\nStudy of market and marketing of agricultural produce.\\nThis programme will also help in enhancing students’ employability\\nTo enhance an understanding of the impact of globalization and diversity on\\nStudents will be able to understand and analyze the current developments in agriculture and how they affect their future in agriculture.\\nStudents will be able to recognize and examine the relationships between inputs and outputs in their agricultural field to make effective and profitable decisions.\\nStudents will understand how all aspects of agriculture combine and are used by scientists, marketers, and producers.\\nStudents will be able to demonstrate critical thinking and problem solving skills as they apply the same to a variety of animal and or plant production systems.\\nA wide range of job opportuniti\n--- https://www.mangalayatan.ac.in/department-of-agriculture/masters-of-science-agriculture/ ---\nDuration\\n2 years undergraduate professional degree\\nEligibility\\nB.sc(H) Agriculture with 50% Marks\\nFees\\nTotal 60,000/- Year INR Only\\nMasters of Science (Agriculture)\\nWhy MUJ for this course\\nM.Sc. Agriculture has been envisaged as one of the most prestigious programs of the University. The University intends to bring about positive changes in the lives of the people of Mahakaushal region through modern agriculture practices. That is why the University has developed state of the art infrastructure and hired highly qualified faculty for this program to groom successful agriculturists and agriculture scientists of the future.\\nThe specializations of this program are under:\\nAgronomy\\nBiotechnology\\nAgricultural Economics & Farm Management\\nPlant Physiology\\nEntomology\\nExtension Education\\nHorticulture\\nPlant Breeding & Genetics\\nPlant Pathology\\nSoil Science & Agricultural Chemistry\\nForestry\\nFood Science & Technology\\nProgram Overview\\nM.Sc. Agriculture programs intends to acquaint the students with major aspects of the trade like plant Biology & Pathology, Plantation Management, Agricultural Machinery, Biochemistry, Livestock Management, Agri-Business & Marketing etc.\\nIt also aims at acquainting students with latest technological advances to increase agricultural productivity.\\nThrough extensive practical sessions the program intends to enable the students to apply advanced techniques in the field.\\nAfter successful completion of this program, the student will be able to:\\nApply latest farming technologies and practices\\nProvide consultancy to farmers, i.e. dissemination of knowledge and advanced techniques, thereby increasing their income\\nAnalyze the demand of various agricultural produce and adopt appropriate marketing strategy.\\nEnhance their employability.\\nUnderstand the implications of globalization and diversity in modern agricultural organizations.\\nTo recognize the relationship between inputs and outputs in the farms thereby enabling them to make effective and profitable decisions.\\nApply critical thinking and problem solving skills to a variety of plant and animal production systems.\\nResearch Officer\\nQuality Assurance Officer\\nAgriculture Officer\\nAgriculture Loan Officer (in Banks)\\nProduction Manager\\nOperations Manager\\nFarm Manager\\nFaculty in Institutions offering Agriculture Science\\nSales Officer\\nAgricultural Scientist\\nResearch Scientist\\nFood Processing officer\\nAgri-products Marketing officer\\nCandidate seeking admission to B.Sc. (H) Agriculture program should have passed 10+2 (PCB/ PCM) with minimum 50% marks or equivalent grade from a recognize Board or Institutions.\\nDuration of this program is two years. The program is divided into four semesters of 6 months each.\\nFAQ's\\nIf you are not a graduate in Agriculture Science, you may pursue Diploma in Agriculture.\\nYes, agricultural programs can be pursued through distance learning. Popular open universities such as Indira Gandhi National Open University (IGNOU) offer part-time Agriculture Science programs through distance learning mode.\\nSome of the popular Agriculture branches in which courses are offered to students include Crop Production, Agricultural Engineering, Agronomy, Horticulture, Forestry, Dairy Technology and Fisheries Science.\\nSome of the popular Agriculture job profiles include Agriculture Officer, Agriculture Scientist, Farm Manager, Production Manager, Agronomist, Agricultural Engineer, Forester, Arborist and Soil Engineer.\\nFacilities\\nIndustry oriented Curriculum\\nGlobally recognised Programs\\nEco-Friendly Big Campus\\nEminent faculty from Academia & Industry\\nDigital Classroom & Wi-fi Campus\\nUpto 100% Scholarship for meritorious Students\\nIndoor & Outdoor Sports facility\\nCentrally AC Classrooms\\nDynamic Placement Cell\\nScholarships & Stipend from Government\\nCore values Adherence & Disciplined Environment\\nDigital Classroom & Wi-fi Campus\\nExcellent Library, Laboratories at Hi-tech Computer Labs\\nIndustrial / Educational Tour for hands-on Learning\n--- https://www.mangalayatan.ac.in/department-of-agriculture/m-sc-forestry/ ---\nDuration\\nTwo years comprising 4 semesters,\\nEligibility\\nB.sc(H) Agriculture with 50% Mark\\nFees\\nINR 60,000/Year Only\\nAbout Programme\\nConsidering the future of the world’s forests, there isthe great significance of higher education in the domain of forestry.Students who want to make career in this field should possess adequate skills to meet future challenges. Higher education in Forestry, M.sc Forestry are among the courses that are gaining greater significance in the era of climate change and global warming because of the necessity to enhance forest production, conserve natural resources, and protecting the environment.\\nM.sc Forestry programme at Mangalayatan University Jabalpur is a postgraduation programme of two years focused on the study of forests and its uses. During the programme, students acquire advanced knowledge in the field of Biology, Business Economics, Logistics, Forest Ecology, etc.\\nWhy Choose Mangalayatan University Jabalpur for M.sc Forestry?\\nMangalayatan University Jabalpur is the best University in Jabalpur, highly acclaimed and coveted for higher education in the domain ofagriculture and its allied areas\\nThe programme exposes students to practical forestry management experience and high-quality applied research that aims to bring positive change to the natural world\\nThe programme equips students with excellent technical acumen and problem-solving skills which make them globally competitive and inspires for higher studies and research and development\\nStudents get Hands-on Training (HOT) and internship opportunities at coveted Forest Research Institutes\\nThe University also provides practical cum demonstration farms for the students and raises their experiments under the supervision of highly experienced faculty & technical staff\\nProgram Overview\\nUpon completion of M.sc Forestry, candidates can make career as an Entomologist. An Entomologiststudies city, forest, agricultural medical, and veterinary pests and their management. Generally, Entomologists are employed by small commercial enterprises and big industrial organizations\\nM.Sc. Forestry graduates can make career as Ethologist. An Ethologist has the expertise to identify animal behavior. An Ethologist studies the interaction between specific animals, how they grow or become extinct\\nCandidates who have M.sc Forestry degree can make career as aSilviculturist. Silviculturistresearch on concerning issues of woodland propagation, tree growth rate, consequences of thinning on wooded area yield, period of seed viability\\nCandidates can appear in the Indian Forest Service examination, which is conducted by UPSC\\nEducational Institutions.\\nSeed and Nursery Companies.\\nForest Services.\\nFood Companies.\\nLand Management Agencies.\\nPlant Health Inspection Services.\\nPlant Resources Laboratories.\\nBiotechnology Firms.\\nEducational Institutions.\\nSeed and Nursery Companies.\\nFood Companies.\\nLand Management Agencies.\\nPlant Health Inspection Services.\\nPlant Resources Laboratories.\\nBiotechnology Firms.\\nAny candidate with a bachelor’s degree in Forestry or equivalent from a recognized institute eligible for M.sc Forestry admission\\nFrequently Asked Questions (FAQs)\\nThe program generally lasts 2 years.\\nStudents learn advanced forest management, wildlife conservation, ecology, and environmental policy.\\nYes. Students engage in field research, surveys, and dissertation projects.\\nYou will develop expertise in conservation planning, forest resource management, and environmental analysis.\\nGraduates can work in forestry departments, environmental organizations, research institutes, and academic institutions.\\nFacilities\\nIndustry oriented Curriculum\\nGlobally recognised Programs\\nEco-Friendly Big Campus\\nEminent faculty from Academia & Industry\\nDigital Classroom & Wi-fi Campus\\nUpto 100% Scholarship for meritorious Students\\nIndoor & Outdoor Sports facility\\nCentrally AC Classrooms\\nDynamic Placement Cell\\nScholarships & Stipend from Government\\nCore values Adherence & Disciplined Environment\\nDigital Classroom & Wi-fi Campus\\nExcellent Library, Laboratories at Hi-tech Computer Labs\\nIndustrial / Educational Tour for hands-on Learning\n--- https://www.mangalayatan.ac.in/department-of-agriculture/m-sc-horticulture/ ---\nDuration\\n2 Years Programme\\nEligibility\\nB.sc (H) Agriculture with 50% Marks\\nFees\\nTotal 120,000 INR\\nM. Sc. Horticulture\\nM.sc Horticulture programme of Mangalayatan University Jabalpur is a judicious blend of practical and theoretical education in which students are taught about the cultivation and primary processing of plants. During two years of education, students acquire comprehensive knowledge of horticulture, natural sciences and advanced knowledge of fruits, medicinal plants, vegetables, etc.\\nCore subjects are taught in M.sc Agriculture programme are Tropical and Dry land Horticulture, Sub-Tropical and Temperate Fruit Production, Principles of Plant Physiology, Fertilizer Technology, Soil Chemistry, Statistical Methods for Agricultural Research, Soil Fertility and Fertilizer Use, etc.\\nWhy Choose Mangalayatan University Jabalpur for M. Sc Horticulture?\\nMangalayatan University Jabalpur is the best private University in Jabalpur , dedicated to provide the highest quality of education in the field of agriculture and its allied areas\\nsc Agriculture programme is designed in such a way in which the top-notch emphasis is given to the research and assignment for experimental learning\\nThe University has state-of-the-art laboratories with diverse horticulture tools consisting of shovels, spades, hose pipes, sprinklers, etc.\\nAt the University, students are exposed to reputed specialized academic and research institutions, industries and real farming conditions\\nThrough guest lectures and seminars, the University promises the great viable methods to impart knowledge to its students\\nThe University has highly-qualified and inspiring academicians, some of who are at the forefront of their fields\\nThe University library has been enriched with a number of books, e-books, and learning resources\\nProgram Overview\\nHorticulture prepares students to understand and improve Agri-horticultural productivity, manage processes & products and improve their employability and entrepreneurial skills in agriculture and its allied areas\\nThe programme opens up splendid career avenues in the field of academic research including soil science, plant breeding, genetic engineering, plant biochemistry, plant physiology, etc.\\nThere is a great demand for M.sc Horticulture candidates in public and private sectors. In private sector, they are appointed as Project supervisor, Foreman, Horticultural training manager. Government sectors like Food Corporation of India (FCI), research institutes release exclusive vacancies for M.sc Horticulture degree holders\\nIndian Agricultural Research Institute\\nNational Seeds Corporation Limited\\nState Farms Corporation of India\\nFood Corporation of India\\nCentral Institute of Cotton Research\\nNABARD and other banks\\nFruit cultivation Firm.\\nVegetable cultivation Firm.\\nPlantation and spice crop cultivation.\\nVegetable hybrid seed production.\\nCut flower production and floriculture units.\\nNursery rising.\\nTissue culture laboratories.\\nMarketing of horticultural products and produce.\\nProcessing of horticultural produce.\\nGovernment development departments.\\nAncillary services\\nResearch and educational base institutions.\\nFrequently Asked Questions (FAQs)\\nThe course is generally completed in 2 years.\\nCandidates with a bachelor’s degree in horticulture or a related agricultural discipline are eligible.\\nStudents study crop improvement, protected cultivation, post-harvest technology, and horticultural research.\\nYes. Research projects and dissertation work are important components of the course.\\nGraduates can work as researchers, horticulture officers, consultants, academicians, and agribusiness professionals.\\nFacilities\\nIndustry oriented Curriculum\\nGlobally recognised Programs\\nEco-Friendly Big Campus\\nEminent faculty from Academia & Industry\\nDigital Classroom & Wi-fi Campus\\nUpto 100% Scholarship for meritorious Students\\nIndoor & Outdoor Sports facility\\nCentrally AC Classrooms\\nDynamic Placement Cell\\nScholarships & Stipend from Government\\nCore values Adherence & Disciplined Environment\\nDigital Classroom & Wi-fi Campus\\nExcellent Library, Laboratories at Hi-tech Computer Labs\\nIndustrial / Educational Tour for hands-on Learning\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
