ears, elective courses of the various specializations will be offered alongwith the core courses, some of the specializations offered with this program are Criminal Law, Business & Corporate Law, Labour Law, International Law, Cyber Law etc.\n200: The program also requires practical exposure to the legal exposure. The Students are required to undergo intern ship/training in the industry, legal firm or under a senior advocate so that they are able to face the challenges and requirements of the job/profession after passing out.\n201: Program Objective\n205: Program Outcomes\n206: After successful completion of LLB(H), BALLB or B.ComLLB program, a student will be able to;\n213: Eligibility\n225: The University intends to groom highly competent legal professionals as there is a huge demand for such professionals. Recognizing that good communication and presentation skill is essential for success in the legal profession, additional courses have been incorporated in curricula of these programs to develop these skills in the students. The University has also set a Court Room in the campus to give our students an exposure to the legal practice.\n227: How is B.Com. LLB different from BA LLB ?\n228: The major difference between both the two programs is that the BA LLB offers subjects of Humanities along with the law subjects and, BCom LLB offers subjects of Commerce along with the law subjects.\n229: What are the subjects in BCom LLB program?\n230: In BCom LLB course, commerce subjects like Accounting, Business Studies, Economics, Taxation are included along with the law subjects such as IPR, Environmental Law, Law of Torts, Company Law, Legal Writing, etc.\n231: What career opportunities are available after BCom LLB?\n232: After completing BCom LLB, one can pursue a career in corporate law firms, public sector undertakings, government organisations as well as start own law firms since he/ she has already studied the subjects related to business and commerce.\n233: Is CLAT compulsory for BA LLB?\n235: What can I do after BA LLB?\n236: You can become a lawyer, advocate, paralegal, legal counsellor, legal administrator, law officer, law associate, public prosecutor, judge, etc. If you wish to study further, you can do LLM (Master of Laws) and other professional specialized certificate and diploma courses.\n239: Globally recognised Programs\n265: National Ragging Prevention Programme\n268: Top Programmes\n304: BA LLB\n305: LLB (Hons)\n306: LLM 1 Year\n307: LLM 2Year Law Course\n338: M.Sc. Forestry (Agro-Forestry)\n339: M.Sc. Forestry (Mushroom Technology)\n340: M.Sc. Forestry (Medicinal and Aromatic Technology)\n344: BA in Political Science\n345: BA in Sociology\n346: BA in Psychology\n347: BA in Economics\n348: BA English\n371: National Ragging Prevention Programme\n427: National Ragging Prevention Programme\n=== department-of-legal-studies-research/llm-1year-law-course/\n0: Join Master of Law (LLM) Admission 2026 – Best University in Jabalpur Mangalayatan University Jabalpur - Best University in Madhya Pradesh\n33: BA LLB\n34: LLB (Hons)\n35: LLM 1 Year\n36: LLM 2Year Law Course\n67: M.Sc. Forestry (Agro-Forestry)\n68: M.Sc. Forestry (Mushroom Technology)\n69: M.Sc. Forestry (Medicinal and Aromatic Technology)\n73: BA in Political Science\n74: BA in Sociology\n75: BA in Psychology\n76: BA in Economics\n77: BA English\n100: National Ragging Prevention Programme\n156: National Ragging Prevention Programme\n180: Duration\n182: Eligibility\n187: The LLM course at Mangalayatan University, Jabalpur, is a postgraduate degree that imparts advanced legal education to graduates interested in becoming more specialized in a particular area of law. Structured with scholarly rigor and professional focus, the course endows students with advanced specialized knowledge and research capabilities, enabling them to excel as legal scholars, practitioners, and policymakers.\n188: The program enables students to specialize in different areas of law, for example, constitutional law, criminal law, business law, human rights, or international law. With a well-designed curriculum, the students are provided with in-depth knowledge of legal principles, judicial procedures, and modern-day legal issues. This specialization enables them to solve intricate problems and make valuable contributions to the legal career and society as a whole.\n189: Mangalayatan University, Jabalpur, offers a dynamic learning environment for LLM students, emphasizing research, analysis, and practical application. The students participate in seminars, debates, case studies, and dissertation projects, which improve their skills to critically analyze legal systems and provide solutions. The university’s teaching faculty, comprising experienced academicians and practitioners, guides students in theoretical and practical applications of law.\n190: The graduates of the LLM program are best suited for versatile career opportunities. They can serve as senior advocates, legal consultants in multinational organizations, law professors, or policy analysts. The degree also presents chances to work in government.\n191: organizations, NGOs, and international organizations. Furthermore, for those who wish to pursue doctoral research (Ph.D.) in law, the LLM is a bridge.\n192: By joining the LLM program of Mangalayatan University, Jabalpur, students achieve a life-changing educational experience that enhances their minds, ensures improved career opportunities, and enables them to become leaders in the legal field.\n193: Program Overview\n194: Program Educational Objectives\n195: Program Outcomes\n196: Eligibility\n198: Program Educational Objectives\n202: Program Outcomes\n203: After successful completion of LLB(H), BALLB or B.Com LLB program, a student will be able to;\n210: Eligibility\n222: The University intends to groom highly competent legal professionals as there is a huge demand for such professionals. Recognizing that good communication and presentation skill