 Year 2024-2025\n163: Holiday Calendar Year 2026\n164: Annual Report Expand\n165: Annual Report 2020 -2021\n166: Annual Report 2021 -2022\n167: Annual Report 2022 -2023\n168: Annual Report 2023 -2024\n169: Annual Report 2024 – 2025\n170: NewsLetter Expand\n171: MUJ Newsletter Jan. 2025 – June 2025 – Vol. 1 & Vol 2\n172: MUJ Newsletter July 2025 – Sept. 2025 – Vol. 3\n173: MUJ Newsletter Oct. 2025 – Dec. 2025 – Vol. 4\n174: MUJ News Letter Vol. 5 Jan-March 2026\n175: Free Legal Aid\n176: Public Self-Disclosure\n177: Refer a Friend\n178: Facebook X Instagram Linkedin YouTube\n179: Toggle Menu\n180: Duration\n181: 2 year which consists of 2 semesters\n182: Eligibility\n183: 10+2 or Equivalent in Agriculture or Science\n184: Fees\n185: Total 30,000 / Year INR Only\n186: About Programme\n187: This program focuses on basics of Agriculture, Biology, and Technology. It also focuses on allied areas including Poultry Farming, Horticulture, Meteorology, etc. It also deals with the various forms of Technology which helps to improve agricultural productivity. Pursuing a career in agriculture is not easy, one has to love the soil and the nature, needs courage to get the hands dirty for food and witness the miracle of crop life being part of our culture and tradition. So, “Live your passion and culture together”.\n188: To be honest, qualified professionals are always valued, when it comes to agriculture sector. Thus, it is evident that there is more than just one reason to pursue this course!\n189: Why MUJ for this course\n196: Eligibility\n197: Duration\n228: Eligibility\n230: Duration\n231: Diploma in Agriculture is a one year program which can be pursued by a student who is interested in taking up agriculture as his/her profession. The duration of the program is 1 year which consists of 2 semesters.\n263: Eligibility\n265: Duration\n266: Diploma in Agriculture is a one year program which can be pursued by a student who is interested in taking up agriculture as his/her profession. The duration of the program is 1 year which consists of 2 semesters.\n=== department-of-agriculture/b-sc-h-agriculture/\n0: B.Sc Agriculture Admission 2026: Course Details, Eligibility Mangalayatan University Jabalpur - Best University in Madhya Pradesh\n1: Skip to content\n160: Statutory Committees\n161: Annual University Calendar Expand\n162: Academic Calendar Year 2024-2025\n163: Holiday Calendar Year 2026\n164: Annual Report Expand\n165: Annual Report 2020 -2021\n166: Annual Report 2021 -2022\n167: Annual Report 2022 -2023\n168: Annual Report 2023 -2024\n169: Annual Report 2024 – 2025\n170: NewsLetter Expand\n171: MUJ Newsletter Jan. 2025 – June 2025 – Vol. 1 & Vol 2\n172: MUJ Newsletter July 2025 – Sept. 2025 – Vol. 3\n173: MUJ Newsletter Oct. 2025 – Dec. 2025 – Vol. 4\n174: MUJ News Letter Vol. 5 Jan-March 2026\n175: Free Legal Aid\n176: Public Self-Disclosure\n177: Refer a Friend\n178: Facebook X Instagram Linkedin YouTube\n179: Toggle Menu\n180: Duration\n181: 4 years undergraduate professional degree\n182: Eligibility\n183: Passed 10+2 (PCB/ PCM) with minimum 50% marks\n184: Fees\n185: Total 72,000/- Year INR Only\n186: B.Sc. (H) Agriculture\n187: B.Sc. (H) Agriculture is a 4 years undergraduate professional degree program offered by various government and private universities in India. The program is divided into 8 semesters so that students can complete this program in a periodical manner. In the first year of the program, students will learn the basics of plants, the economics of agriculture and courses of humanities & social science. In the second and third years, they will study core agriculture engineering, entomology, and microbiology etc. They will also get their skills strengthened in communication and entrepreneurship. In the final year, they will get hands-on experience practically on-field through Agronomy and Agricultural Statistics.\n188: Programme Overview\n189: Eligibility\n194: Eligibility\n274: What is the duration of the B.Sc. Agriculture program?\n=== department-of-agriculture/b-sc-hons-horticulture/\n0: B.Sc (Hons.) Horticulture Admission 2026: Course Details & Fees Mangalayatan University Jabalpur - Best University in Madhya Pradesh\n1: Skip to content\n160: Statutory Committees\n161: Annual University Calendar Expand\n162: Academic Calendar Year 2024-2025\n163: Holiday Calendar Year 2026\n164: Annual Report Expand\n165: Annual Report 2020 -2021\n166: Annual Report 2021 -2022\n167: Annual Report 2022 -2023\n168: Annual Report 2023 -2024\n169: Annual Report 2024 – 2025\n170: NewsLetter Expand\n171: MUJ Newsletter Jan. 2025 – June 2025 – Vol. 1 & Vol 2\n172: MUJ Newsletter July 2025 – Sept. 2025 – Vol. 3\n173: MUJ Newsletter Oct. 2025 – Dec. 2025 – Vol. 4\n174: MUJ News Letter Vol. 5 Jan-March 2026\n175: Free Legal Aid\n176: Public Self-Disclosure\n177: Refer a Friend\n178: Facebook X Instagram Linkedin YouTube\n179: Toggle Menu\n180: Duration\n181: 4 years undergraduate professional degree\n182: Eligibility\n183: Passed 10+2 (PCB/ PCM) with minimum 50% marks\n184: Fees\n185: Total 72,000/- Year INR Only\n186: About B.Sc (Hons.) horticulture\n187: In the context of nutritional security and economic stability, there is a great significance of fruits, vegetables, flowers, and crops. Today, in the era of globalization and economic liberalization,horticulture sector has immense potentialin poverty alleviation, increasing farmers’ income and sustaining a large number of Agro-based industries which generate a large number of employment opportunities. Keeping view of immense potential of the horticulture sector, the Government of India is making robust policies and significant changes in the existing system to uplift and strengthen the sector.\n188: The opening of global trade in the horticulture sector has encouraged manyto diversify their activities with horticulture crops and also created a great demand of professionals to help in the development of the horticulture sector in the country. Keeping this thing in mind, Mangalayatan University Jabalpur has started a full-fledgedfour year undergraduate programme B.sc (Hons) Horticulture.\n189: The curriculum of B.sc (Hons) Horticulture includes theory and practical education over eight semestersfocused on developing scientific approach and business skills in students which are essential for them to succeedin the commercial horticulture sector. The programme integrates the basic sciences, humanities, horticulture, allied sciences and horticultural engineering.Through the programme students acquainted with various facets of horticulture and its related specializations in the well-equipped laboratories as well as in real environment in related industries and farming.\n218: What is the duration of the course?\n=== department-of-agriculture/b-sc-hons-forestry/\n0: Apply Now for B.Sc Forestry Admission 2026 – Top University Mangalayatan University Jabalpur - Best University in Madhya Pradesh\n1: Skip to content\n160: Statutory Committees\n161: Annual University Calendar Expand\n162: Academic Calendar Year 2024-2025\n163: Holiday Calendar Year 2026\n164: Annual Report Expand\n165: Annual Report 2020 -2021\n166: Annual Report 2021 -2022\n167: Annual Report 2022 -2023\n168: Annual Report 2023 -2024\n169: Annual Report 2024 – 2025\n170: NewsLetter Expand\n171: MUJ Newsletter Jan. 2025 – June 2025 – Vol. 1 & Vol 2\n172: MUJ Newsletter July 2025 – Sept. 2025 – Vol. 3\n173: MUJ Newsletter Oct. 2025 – Dec. 2025 – Vol. 4\n174: MUJ News Letter Vol. 5 Jan-March 2026\n175: Free Legal Aid\n176: Public Self-Disclosure\n177: Refer a Friend\n178: Facebook X Instagram Linkedin YouTube\n179: Toggle Menu\n180: Duration\n181: 4 years undergraduate professional degree\n182: Eligibility\n183: Passed 10+2 (PCB/ PCM) with minimum 50% marks\n184: Fees\n185: Total 72,000/- Year INR Only\n186: About B.Sc (Hons.) Forestry\n187: Do you want to save and shape the future of the environment? Do you want to make an exciting and challenging career in the lap of nature? Then, B.sc (Hons) Forestry is an appropriate programme for you. B.sc (Hons) Forestry is an undergraduate programme of four years focused to impart theoretical and practical knowledge in all areas of forestry.The programme is an excellent blend of practical and theoretical education in which students get acquainted with various scientific, technical, and economic strategies to forest estate to achieve multiple objectives including the production of various forest products like timber, gum, resin, tanbark, andother raw materials.\n188: Some major subjects taught in B.sc (Hons) Forestry areFundamentals of Geology and Soil Science, Plant Biochemistry and Biotechnology, Introductory Botany, Basic Mathematics, Principles of Plant physiology, Elementary Statistic and Computer Application, Chemistry and Fertility of Soils, Wood Science and Technology, etc.\n189: Eligibility & Duration\n193: Eligibility & Duration\n249: What is the duration of the course?\n=== department-of-agriculture/masters-of-science-agriculture/\n0: Join MSc Agriculture Admission 2026 – Best University Mangalayatan University Jabalpur - Best University in Madhya Pradesh\n1: Skip to content\n160: Statutory Committees\n161: Annual University Calendar Expand\n162: Academic Calendar Year 2024-2025\n163: Holiday Calendar Year 2026\n164: Annual Report Expand\n165: Annual Report 2020 -2021\n166: Annual Report 2021 -2022\n167: Annual Report 2022 -2023\n168: Annual Report 2023 -2024\n169: Annual Report 2024 – 2025\n170: NewsLetter Expand\n171: MUJ Newsletter Jan. 2025 – June 2025 – Vol. 1 & Vol 2\n172: MUJ Newsletter July 2025 – Sept. 2025 – Vol. 3\n173: MUJ Newsletter Oct. 2025 – Dec. 2025 – Vol. 4\n174: MUJ News Letter Vol. 5 Jan-March 2026\n175: Free Legal Aid\n176: Public Self-Disclosure\n177: Refer a Friend\n178: Facebook X Instagram Linkedin YouTube\n179: Toggle Menu\n180: Duration\n181: 2 years undergraduate professional degree\n182: Eligibility\n183: B.sc(H) Agriculture with 50% Marks\n184: Fees\n185: Total 60,000/- Year INR Only\n186: Masters of Science (Agriculture)\n187: M.Sc. Agriculture is a two years postgraduate degree program. This is an applied program which aims at providing in depth theoretical knowledge alongwith hands on experience of advanced practices of agriculture. As the agriculture sector has immense potential for growth, a major thrust area in this field is research and development. Over the past few decades, agriculture sector has witnessed sea change with the introduction of modern techniques and farming practices. This program is meant for those students who want to take up agriculture as their profession as entrepreneurs in agri-business or those who want to build their career in agri-business or allied sectors, or those who want to pursue research in this field as research scientists.\n188: Why MUJ for this course\n189: M.Sc. Agriculture has been envisaged as one of the most prestigious programs of the University. The University intends to bring about positive changes in the lives of the people of Mahakaushal region through modern agriculture practices. That is why the University has developed state of the art infrastructure and hired highly qualified faculty for this program to groom successful agriculturists and agriculture scientists of the future.\n208: Eligibility\n209: Duration\n238: Eligibility\n240: Duration\n241: Duration of this program is two years. The program is divided into four semesters of 6 months each.\n=== department-of-agriculture/m-sc-horticulture/\n0: Apply For M.Sc Horticulture Admission 2026 – Top University in Jabalpur Mangalayatan University Jabalpur - Best University in Madhya Pradesh\n1: Skip to content\n160: Statutory Committees\n161: Annual University Calendar Expand\n162: Academic Calendar Year 2024-2025\n163: Holiday Calendar Year 2026\n164: Annual Report Expand\n165: Annual Report 2020 -2021\n166: Annual Report 2021 -2022\n167: Annual Report 2022 -2023\n168: Annual Report 2023 -2024\n169: Annual Report 2024 – 2025\n170: NewsLetter Expand\n171: MUJ Newsletter Jan. 2025 – June 2025 – Vol. 1 & Vol 2\n172: MUJ Newsletter July 2025 – Sept. 2025 – Vol. 3\n173: MUJ Newsletter Oct. 2025 – Dec. 2025 – Vol. 4\n174: MUJ News Letter Vol. 5 Jan-March 2026\n175: Free Legal Aid\n176: Public Self-Disclosure\n177: Refer a Friend\n178: Facebook X Instagram Linkedin YouTube\n179: Toggle Menu\n180: Duration\n181: 2 Years Programme\n182: Eligibility\n183: B.sc (H) Agriculture with 50% Marks\n184: Fees\n185: Total 120,000 INR\n186: M. Sc. Horticulture\n187: Today, in the era of globalization as an academic discipline and the context of career scope, the significance of horticulture education has enhanced manifold. Today, higher education in horticulture like M.sc Horticulture not only opens up splendid career avenues but is also gaining greater significance to enhance horticulture production and profitability, conserve natural resources and in protecting the environment through innovative and safer high-value production, processing and trade systems.\n188: M.sc Horticulture programme of Mangalayatan University Jabalpur is a judicious blend of practical and theoretical education in which students are taught about the cultivation and primary processing of plants. During two years of education, students acquire comprehensive knowledge of horticulture, natural sciences and advanced knowledge of fruits, medicinal plants, vegetables, etc.\n189: Core subjects are taught in M.sc Agriculture programme are Tropical and Dry land Horticulture, Sub-Tropical and Temperate Fruit Production, Principles of Plant Physiology, Fertilizer Technology, Soil Chemistry, Statistical Methods for Agricultural Research, Soil Fertility and Fertilizer Use, etc.\n202: Eligibility\n227: Eligibility\n230: What is the duration of the M.Sc. Horticulture program?\n=== department-of-agriculture/m-sc-forestry/\n0: Enroll Now for M.Sc Forestry Admission 2026 – Mangalayatan University Mangalayatan University Jabalpur - Best University in Madhya Pradesh\n1: Skip to content\n160: Statutory Committees\n161: Annual University Calendar Expand\n162: Academic Calendar Year 2024-2025\n163: Holiday Calendar Year 2026\n164: Annual Report Expand\n165: Annual Report 2020 -2021\n166: Annual Report 2021 -2022\n167: Annual Report 2022 -2023\n168: Annual Report 2023 -2024\n169: Annual Report 2024 – 2025\n170: NewsLetter Expand\n171: MUJ Newsletter Jan. 2025 – June 2025 – Vol. 1 & Vol 2\n172: MUJ Newsletter July 2025 – Sept. 2025 – Vol. 3\n173: MUJ Newsletter Oct. 2025 – Dec. 2025 – Vol. 4\n174: MUJ News Letter Vol. 5 Jan-March 2026\n175: Free Legal Aid\n176: Public Self-Disclosure\n177: Refer a Friend\n178: Facebook X Instagram Linkedin YouTube\n179: Toggle Menu\n180: Duration\n181: Two years comprising 4 semesters,\n182: Eligibility\n183: B.sc(H) Agriculture with 50% Mark\n184: Fees\n185: INR 60,000/Year Only\n186: About Programme\n187: Considering the future of the world’s forests, there isthe great significance of higher education in the domain of forestry.Students who want to make career in this field should possess adequate skills to meet future challenges. Higher education in Forestry, M.sc Forestry are among the courses that are gaining greater significance in the era of climate change and global warming because of the necessity to enhance forest production, conserve natural resources, and protecting the environment.\n188: M.sc Forestry programme at Mangalayatan University Jabalpur is a postgraduation programme of two years focused on the study of forests and its uses. During the programme, students acquire advanced knowledge in the field of Biology, Business Economics, Logistics, Forest Ecology, etc.\n189: In addition, the programme enables students to acquire advanced knowledge in Biology, Business Economics, Environmental Sciences, Logistics, Ecoinformatics, information technology, forest Ecology control and use of forest resources, forest bio-economic business, and policy. In the final year, according to interest students can choose subjects like climate change, prevention of damage to forests resulting from insects and fungi, problems associated with the exploitation of tropical forests, wood harvesting and logistics, and so forth.\n200: Eligibility\n223: Eligibility\n226: What is the duration of the M.Sc. Forestry program?\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
