e department of Science currently runs undergraduate programs B.Sc .(H)Information Technology ,B.Sc. Forensic Science which are 3year course programs and some post graduate level like M.Sc. Information Technology, M.Sc. Forensic Science etc. which are 3 year course programs.\n12: The Department of Science offers programs are blended with the latest industry and best business practices that equips students with in-depth subject knowledge and sublime business acumen that supports an advanced career in the field of Science. Below are the salient features of our Science programs:\n13: Varied courses in Science like Forensic Science at both graduate and post graduate level, to offer best career progression.\n14: Theoretical and research based learning incorporates practical, hands-on experience through laboratory work are best tools for imparting technical programs. Theoretical knowledge to real-world problems helps students to acquire knowledge in the form of practical experience.\n15: Strong industry collaboration with top companies to ensure that our courses are relevant and according to the need of the industry.\n19: These courses are designed according to the demand in the field of Science and ever-evolving dynamics of corporate culture, changing business environment and as per the need of the industry.\n20: Science Programmes Offered by Mangalayatan University Jabalpur\n22: B.Sc. (H) Information Technology\n23: Eligibility : 10+2 or Equivalent\n24: Duration : 3 Years\n25: B.Sc. Forensic Science\n26: Eligibility : 10+2 or Equivalent\n27: Duration : 3Years\n28: M.Sc. Information Technology\n29: Eligibility : B.Sc. IT\n30: Duration : 2 Years\n32: Eligibility : B.Sc. Forensic Science\n33: Duration : 2 Years\n=== admissions/btech-electrical-electronics-engineering-courses.php (   12580 bytes)\n0: B.Tech Electrical & Electronics Engineering - Mangalayatan University Jabalpur\n1: Apply Online for Admission 2026-27\n4: B.Tech Electrical & Electronics Engineering\n6: Mangalayatan University Jabalpur B.Tech Electrical & Electronics Engineering\n8: B.Tech Electrical & Electronics Engineering\n9: Bachelor of Technology - B.Tech Electrical & Electronics Engineering is a popular undergraduate degree program that focuses on the study of electrical and electronics systems, their design, analysis, and application. This field combines the principles of electrical engineering and electronics engineering, preparing students for careers in various industries related to electrical power, electronics, telecommunications, and more.\n10: During a B.Tech Electrical Engineering a wide range of subjects are studied:\n13: Core Electrical and Electronics Engineering: Electrical Circuit Analysis, Electrical Machines, Power Systems, Control Systems, Analog and Digital Electronics, Microprocessors, Signals and Systems, Electromagnetic Theory, Power Electronics, and Instrumentation.\n14: Specialized Subjects: Depending on your interests and the curriculum of your university, you may have the option to choose elective courses in areas such as Renewable Energy Systems, Robotics, Embedded Systems, VLSI Design, Communication Systems, and more.\n15: Laboratory Work: Hands-on experience is an integral part of the program, and you will have the opportunity to work in electrical and electronics engineering laboratories to gain practical skills and apply theoretical concepts.\n16: Upon completing a B.Tech in Electrical and Electronics Engineering, you can pursue a wide range of career paths. Some common job roles include electrical engineer, electronics engineer, power systems engineer, control systems engineer, design engineer, research and development engineer, and telecommunications engineer. You can work in industries such as power generation and distribution, electronics manufacturing, telecommunications, automotive, aerospace, renewable energy, and consulting firms.\n17: Moreover, you may choose to pursue higher education such as a Master's degree (M.Tech) or a Ph.D. in specialized areas of electrical and electronics engineering to further enhance your knowledge and career prospects therefore, the aspirant must take engineering course admission.\n23: Embedded Systems: Embedded systems are prevalent in various industries , including automotive, aerospace, healthcare, and industrial automation. Electronics engineers work on designing and programming embedded systems that control and monitor devices and processes.\n30: Programmes Offered\n31: B.Tech Electrical & Electronics Engineering\n32: Eligibility : 10+2\n33: Duration : 4 Years\n=== department-of-information-technology/bachelor-of-science-in-information-technology/ (  298555 bytes)\n0: Start Your Career with BSc.IT Admission 2026 – Top University Mangalayatan University Jabalpur - Best University in Madhya Pradesh\n1: Skip to content\n36: LLM 2Year Law Course\n46: Department of Information Technology Expand\n50: B.Sc. Forensic Science\n61: B.Sc. (H) Agriculture\n62: B.Sc (Hons.) horticulture\n63: B.Sc (Hons.) Forestry\n100: National Ragging Prevention Programme\n156: National Ragging Prevention Programme\n180: Bachelor of Science in Information Technology (B.Sc. in IT)\n181: Duration\n183: Eligibility\n187: About Programme\n188: The world is rapidly transforming through technology, and information technology (IT) has become the backbone of every sector—from education to enterprise and healthcare to hospitality. The Bachelor of Science in Information Technology ( B.Sc . IT) is one of the most sought-after undergraduate programs, offering students a solid foundation in computing, software, data management, and IT systems. Mangalayatan University, Jabalpur, through its Faculty of Science, proudly offers a specialized B.Sc . IT course designed to shape the IT leaders of tomorrow with strong technical expertise, practical skills, and a problem-solving mindset.\n190: Why Choose a B.Sc. in IT as a Career?\n191: Choosing a B.Sc. in IT as a career path means stepping into a future filled with endless opportunities, digital innovation, and societal transformation. Here’s why this program is the right choice for aspiring tech professionals:\n192: Backbone of Modern Industry: In the digital era, information technology is the pillar on which every organization relies. Professionals with a Bachelor of Science in Information Technology play a crucial role in developing software solutions, managing data, and maintaining network systems.\n193: High Demand Across Sectors: From IT companies to finance, e-commerce to logistics, and healthcare to education—B.Sc. IT graduates are in high demand across both public and private sectors, as organizations prioritize digitalization.\n194: Diverse Career Options: Graduates of the B.Sc. IT course can pursue careers in software development, data analytics, cybersecurity, web development, system administration, and much more.\n196: Global Career Scope: A degree in B.Sc. IT opens doors to international opportunities, freelance tech projects, start-ups, and entrepreneurship in the booming tech industry.\n197: Department of Information Technology—Mangalayatan University, Jabalpur\n198: The Faculty of Science at Mangalayatan University, Jabalpur, is committed to developing future-ready professionals through its comprehensive and modern B.Sc . IT course . The department blends theoretical instruction with practical experience, industry exposure, and a research-oriented approach to shape tech-savvy individuals who thrive in fast-paced IT environments.\n199: Bachelor of Science (B.Sc.) in Information Technology\n200: The B.Sc . IT program at Mangalayatan University is a three-year undergraduate course structured into six semesters. It equips students with core knowledge in computing systems, programming languages, data structures, databases, networking, and emerging fields such as artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, and cloud computing.\n202: Eligibility Criteria\n203: Career Opportunities After B.Sc. IT:\n206: Hands-on Programming : Regular coding labs for languages like Python, Java, C++, and web technologies (HTML, CSS, and JavaScript).\n213: Eligibility Criteria\n214: To apply for the B.Sc . IT course , candidates must meet the following criteria:\n218: B.Sc . IT Course Duration:\n219: Total Duration : 3 Years\n222: Career Opportunities After B.Sc. IT:\n223: Graduates of the B.Sc . IT course from Mangalayatan University, Jabalpur, enjoy a wealth of opportunities in the dynamic IT industry. Some prominent job roles include\n236: The Department of Information Technology under the Faculty of Science aims to nurture competent and ethical IT professionals who contribute to technological advancement and societal development.\n242: Why is Mangalayatan University, Jabalpur, the best for B.Sc. IT?\n243: Choosing the right university for your Bachelor of Science in Information Technology is crucial, and Mangalayatan University, Jabalpur, stands out for several compelling reasons:\n246: Industry Tie-Ups and Internship Opportunities: Partnerships with IT companies for hands-on internships, training programs, and placement support.\n250: UGC-Recognized Degree: Globally recognized B.Sc. IT degree with credibility and value in both Indian and international job markets.\n253: In a world where digital literacy is not just a skill but a necessity, the B.Sc . IT course at Mangalayatan University, Jabalpur, acts as a gateway to a bright and promising tech career. With an industry-relevant curriculum, practical approach, and committed faculty, this Bachelor of Science in Information Technology program is your first step toward success in the digital domain.\n255: Take the leap into the digital future—admission for B.Sc . IT is now open at Mangalayatan University, Jabalpur.\n258: Globally recognised Programs\n284: National Ragging Prevention Programme\n287: Top Programmes\n326: LLM 2Year Law Course\n336: Department of Information Technology Toggle child menu Expand\n340: B.Sc. Forensic Science\