 is made to equip students not only with the knowledge to practice law but also with the skills to address intricate business and financial matters that usually involve legal intervention. As industries and business forms expand in India, demand has greatly risen for professionals with the knowledge of commerce and law, rendering this program very relevant.\n189: At Mangalayatan University, Jabalpur, the course syllabus has been carefully planned to offer both theoretical knowledge and practical experience. Students engage in moot courts, legal aid camps, internships, and seminars to realize practical insights into the operations of law and business. The faculty of the university, comprising experienced professionals, helps learners imbibe critical thinking, analytical thinking, and problem-solving capabilities—essential skills for future lawyers and corporate counsellors.\n190: Students graduating from this program have a variety of career opportunities, like corporate law firms, consultancy, litigation, judiciary examinations, taxation law, and even postgraduate studies in law or commerce-related fields.\n191: By opting for the B.Com LLB program at Mangalayatan University, Jabalpur, not only do students get a professional degree, but they also launch the gateway to a future where they can make policies, protect justice, and head organizations with legal and financial acumen.\n192: Program Overview\n193: These 5 years integrated programs are meant for those early birds who decide to pursue their career in Law 10+2 itself. The programs are divided into 10 semesters of 6 months each. Apart from studying the subjects of their stream (Humanities or Commerce), the students also study the courses of Law, in these programs. In order to groom highly competent legal professionals, the programs focus on hands-on training through moot court, internship in the Industry, Legal firms or under some senior lawyer, so that they are able to meet the requirements and challenges of their job/profession effectively.\n194: Program Educational Objectives\n195: Program Outcomes\n196: Eligibility\n197: Career Opportunities\n198: Program Educational Objectives\n199: To provide comprehensive knowledge of Law to the students and the acquaint them with the Indian legal system.\n200: To acquaint the students with the specialized fields of legal profession and to equip them with the required knowledge and skills so that they may become successful professionals.\n201: To provide, highly competent legal professionals to the society and the industry.\n202: Program Outcomes\n203: After successful completion of LLB(H), BALLB or B.Com LLB program, a student will be able to;\n204: Have a comprehensive knowledge and understanding of Indian Legal System.\n205: Deal with various legal issues effectively with proper reasoning & sound arguments.\n206: Pursue legal profession successfully.\n207: Comprehend complex legal issues, analyze critically and take the best decision.\n208: Draft legal documents with precision.\n209: Apply legal knowledge appropriately in the society.\n210: Eligibility\n211: 10+2 Pass in any stream from any recognized Board/Institution with minimum 50% marks (45% for SC/ST candidates) or equivalent grade.\n212: Career Opportunities\n213: A host of career opportunities are available to Law graduates, prominent amon them are:\n214: Legal practice in the Cowds either independently or through a legald firm.\n215: One can apply for various Govt. jobs such as Judicial Magistrate, Public Prosecutor, Solicitors, Legal Advisors, Law Officers etc.\n216: One can also take up jobs like Legal Advisor, Legal Officer etc in various private organizations.\n217: They may work as advocate/legal counsels in various government/private organizations. They are required to advise their employer on various legal issues to protect the employer from any legal implications, and represent their employer in any legal matter.\n218: They can also take up litigations on behalf of their clients managing the entire process e.g. trial investigation, pleadings, discovery etc. They are also required to scrutinize and draft contracts for their company.\n219: As solicitors, they can specialize in a particular field of Law like Tax Law, Family Law, Property Law, Commercial Law, Corporate Law etc. and can offer expert advice to their clients.\n220: Teaching- One can opt for teaching in Govt. and private institutions after pursuing higher studies in the field.\n221: Why MUJ for this course?\n222: The University intends to groom highly competent legal professionals as there is a huge demand for such professionals. Recognizing that good communication and presentation skill is essential for success in the legal profession, additional courses have been incorporated in curricula of these programs to develop these skills in the students. The University has also set a Court Room in the campus to give our students an exposure to the legal practice.\n223: Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ's)\n224: How is B.Com. LLB different from BA LLB ?\n225: The major difference between both the two programs is that the BA LLB offers subjects of Humanities along with the law subjects and, BCom LLB offers subjects of Commerce along with the law subjects.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
